{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3332","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3332","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3332\",\"parent_revision\":\"76976d1053699e1ad5b73a93be15bda20b241475\",\"root_revision\":\"eba9b34524bcbf8f575633d91cfdd37bac5d62f4021244b3d42fdab7e9620e33\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` has two live consumers today \u2014 `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`'s Output Format section and `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md`'s dispatch prompt \u2014 and is about to gain a third via the `dh-meta-docs` skill index. Confirmed drift against `backlog_core/models.py`, verified directly:\\n\\n- `:15` documents a `name:` frontmatter field. `BacklogItem` has no such field \u2014 real fields are `title`/`reference`/`description` (`models.py:1011-1013`).\\n- `:5` \\\"Location\\\" framing says groomed content \\\"lives in the body of `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md`\\\" \u2014 stale extension (real storage is `.yaml`, per `backlog_core/yaml_io.py:84`'s `save_item()` docstring: \\\"Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension\\\"), and this framing doesn't apply at all to `sqlite`/`memory`/`beads` backends, which have no such file-path structure (per `AGENTS.md`'s Backend Providers section).\\n- `:23`'s status vocabulary example (`open|in-progress|done|resolved`) is inconsistent with the vocabulary used elsewhere in the codebase.\\n\\nGoal: correct the frontmatter field list and status vocabulary against `models.py` directly, and rewrite or remove the backend-specific \\\"Location\\\" framing so the doc states only the backend-agnostic content schema (frontmatter shape, body sections, Groomed subsections) that actually gets passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` regardless of which backend is configured. This is actively misleading the grooming agent today, not a cosmetic issue.\\n\\nUser-provided context: surfaced while auditing plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/ for deletion, and while fixing a broken hook that pointed backlog-item-groomer.md at this doc via a nonexistent `.claude/docs/...` path \u2014 see #3329.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:36:04.549629Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1: BacklogItem field list**\\n- verdict: REFUTED\\n- claim: `BacklogItem` has no `name:` field; real fields are `title`/`reference`/`description`\\n- evidence: models.py lines 1011-1013 define three fields: `title: str = \\\"\\\"`, `reference: str = \\\"\\\"`, `description: str = \\\"\\\"`. The doc at line 15 incorrectly shows `name: \\\"Item title\\\"` in the frontmatter example.\\n- source: `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013`\\n\\n**Claim 2: YAML storage format**\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: `save_item()` docstring states storage \\\"Always writes .yaml format regardless of the original file extension.\\\"\\n- evidence: yaml_io.py line 87 explicitly states: \\\"Always writes ``.yaml`` format regardless of the original file extension.\\\"\\n- source: `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/yaml_io.py:87`\\n\\n**Claim 3: Backend file-path structure**\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: `sqlite`/`memory`/`beads` backends have no file-path structure comparable to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md`\\n- evidence: AGENTS.md Backend Providers section documents that only the `github` backend persists to the file-path structure `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md`. For other backends: \\\"Beads, SQLite, and Memory use native storage directly and never read/write backlog YAML or instantiate `FileCache`.\\\"\\n- source: `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` (Backend Providers section)\\n\\n**Claim 4: Status vocabulary**\\n- verdict: REFUTED\\n- claim: The doc's status vocabulary example `open|in-progress|done|resolved` is inconsistent with vocabulary used elsewhere\\n- evidence: models.py line 723 defines `_VALID_STATUSES = {\\\"open\\\", \\\"done\\\", \\\"in-progress\\\", \\\"needs-grooming\\\", \\\"closed\\\"}`. The doc omits `needs-grooming` and `closed`, and incorrectly includes `resolved` which is not a valid status. Additionally, status_registry.py lines 48-50 define label-form statuses `status:needs-grooming` and `status:groomed` which are also absent from the doc.\\n- source: `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:723` and `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/status_registry.py:48-50`\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T09:48:05.104171Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md has field drift vs models.py and backend-specific framing that misleads the groomer agent\\nDate: 2026-08-30\\nGoal: Correct docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md's frontmatter field list and status vocabulary against backlog_core/models.py, and remove backend-specific \\\"Location\\\" framing so the doc is backend-agnostic.\\nConditions:\\n1. BacklogItem's real frontmatter fields are title/reference/description, not name | Status: AVAILABLE (verified: models.py:1011-1013 has no `name` field)\\n2. Real storage format is always .yaml regardless of original extension | Status: AVAILABLE (verified: yaml_io.py save_item() docstring \\\"Always writes .yaml format\\\")\\n3. sqlite/memory/beads backends have no file-path structure, making the \\\"Location\\\" framing backend-specific and misleading | Status: AVAILABLE (verified: AGENTS.md Backend Providers section)\\n4. Real status vocabulary is {open, done, in-progress, needs-grooming, closed} (plus label-form status:groomed / status:needs-grooming), not open|in-progress|done|resolved | Status: AVAILABLE (verified: models.py:723 `_VALID_STATUSES`, status_registry.py, gh_client.py)\\n5. Full set of consumers of this doc | Status: AVAILABLE (verified via grep: agents/backlog-item-groomer.md and skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md are live consumers; docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md cites it as a cross-check source; skills/backlog-tools-administrator/references/domain-registry.md references it via a stale, nonexistent `.claude/docs/...` path \u2014 same broken-path class as #3329, worth flagging to impact-analyst)\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:37:56.730208Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Documentation field drift vs implementation is a traceable failure with clear cause chain \u2014 documentation was not synced when BacklogItem model, storage format, and backend architecture changed.\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Groomer agent reads docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md and receives wrong schema (name: field), wrong storage format (.md instead of .yaml), and backend-specific framing -> agent produces content that doesn't match BacklogItem interface or multi-backend architecture.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-30T10:37:56.730272Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys\\n**Classification**: defect\\n\\n#### Evidence Chain\\n\\n1. CLAIM: BacklogItem model has never documented a `name:` field; real fields are `title`, `reference`, `description`\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 git show 0f3c0fb9b (2026-03-18) BacklogItem first definition shows title/description, not name\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: none (symptom)\\n\\n2. CLAIM: Storage format is always `.yaml` regardless of original extension, not `.md` as documented\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 yaml_io.py:84-87 docstring states \\\"Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension\\\"\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1\\n\\n3. CLAIM: Multi-backend support (sqlite/memory/beads) was implemented in 2026-03-30, making file-path storage framing backend-specific and misleading\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 git log commit a2b56597a \\\"feat(backlog-core): implement pluggable BacklogBackend protocol\\\"\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 2\\n\\n4. CLAIM: Valid status vocabulary is {open, done, in-progress, needs-grooming, closed}, not the documented {open, in-progress, done, resolved}\\n   EVIDENCE: Read \u2014 models.py:723 `_VALID_STATUSES = {\\\"open\\\", \\\"done\\\", \\\"in-progress\\\", \\\"needs-grooming\\\", \\\"closed\\\"}`\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1\\n\\n5. CLAIM: Documentation has not been updated since BacklogItem model, storage layer, and backend architecture changed\\n   EVIDENCE: Bash \u2014 git log shows no recent updates to docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md; git log models.py shows multiple changes in last 5 months\\n   VERIFIED: yes\\n   DEPENDS ON: 1, 2, 3, 4\\n\\n**Root Cause**: No documentation-sync review gate exists in the PR merge process. Code changes to BacklogItem, storage formats, and backend architecture proceed without requiring updates to docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md. No CI check validates documentation accuracy against current implementation. Code reviewers do not cross-check doc accuracy as part of merge gates.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f725fd30f8b0689717c2491782e7c13fc5d1cbcff2b4cf8d33901806cab4f0b8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRe3ZMg\"}"}